Subject: [PATCH 20/30] scsi: ncr53c710: wake Wait Reselect on SIGP

SIGP must branch to the Wait Reselect alternate address when written after
SCRIPTS has parked, as well as when already set on entry to the instruction.
Use the existing resume helper to clear the wait and restart interpretation.

The NEXTSTEP 3.3 PA-RISC driver uses this path during SCSI startup. The
NCR53C710 June 1992 data manual describes SIGP in ISTAT and its read-to-clear
reflection in CTEST2. Regression coverage follows in patch 22.

diff --git a/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c b/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
--- a/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
+++ b/hw/scsi/ncr53c710.c
@@ -1527,6 +1527,10 @@
         }
         if (val & NCR710_ISTAT_ABRT) {
             ncr710_script_dma_interrupt(s, NCR710_DSTAT_ABRT);
+        } else if ((val & NCR710_ISTAT_SIGP) &&
+                   s->waiting == NCR710_WAIT_RESELECT) {
+            s->dsp = s->dnad;
+            ncr710_resume_script(s);
         }
         break;
     case NCR710_CTEST8:
